{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\n`src/rebar/_lib_writes.py` is at **800 lines against the hard 800-line cap**\n(`.github/module-size-limit.txt`), which the CI module-size gate enforces with no allowlist. It\nis one line from red: the next change to any public library write verb fails the build. The\nsibling story adding two optional `create_ticket` arguments must widen two `@overload`\nsignatures, the implementation, and their docstrings — it cannot land until this is relieved.\nThis ticket buys that headroom by concern, not by line count.\n\n## Approach\n\n`_lib_writes` is the **aggregation point for every public library write**, so it grows on two\naxes: a new verb appends a wrapper, and an existing verb gaining an argument widens one in\nplace. The facade split (S3/4532) cut the library **by direction** — writes vs reads vs gates\nvs ops — and that axis is exhausted: the write half alone carries seven concerns. The durable\nfix is to cut it **by concern**, per the `fsck` split (`defaceable-icy-antelope`), which took\ntwo cuts out of one 800-line file.\n\nThe seven concerns present today:\n\n1. **Genesis** — `init_repo`, `create_ticket` (two `@overload`s + impl), `idea`.\n2. **Identity & key material** — `create_identity`, `ensure_identity_for`, `create_placeholder`,\n   `add_identity_key`, `revoke_identity_key`, `use_identity`, `resolve_current_identity`; all\n   delegate to `rebar._commands.identity`, none touches ticket state.\n3. **Status lifecycle** — `transition`, `claim`, `reopen`. The only place in the module that\n   raises `ConcurrencyError`.\n4. **Leaf mutations** — `_python_leaf` and its seven in-module callers `comment`, `edit_ticket`,\n   `link`, `unlink`, `tag`, `untag`, `archive`.\n5. **Session logs** — `append_session_log`, `start_session_log`; own `CommandError` mapping,\n   NOT routed through `_python_leaf`.\n6. **Store maintenance** — `compact`, `attach_commits`.\n7. **Signing** — `sign_manifest`, `verify_signature`, delegating to `rebar.signing`.\n\n**Two cuts**, mirroring `fsck`:\n\n- **`_lib_mutations.py`** takes 4+5+6. Anchored on the `_python_leaf` call graph: one adapter,\n  seven callers, all inside the block, nothing else in this module calling it. Stated honestly,\n  5 and 6 **ride along** as the contiguous remainder of the post-genesis mutation surface, not\n  because they call `_python_leaf`; the strict call-graph subset is ~130 lines and\n  non-contiguous, forcing a scattered cut near the 100-line floor.\n- **`_lib_identity.py`** takes 2+7 — the non-ticket, key-material surface. Identities own\n  OpenSSH key lines, `use_identity`/`resolve_current_identity` select the current one, and\n  signing binds a manifest to the environment key. Stated honestly, signing is ~52 lines and\n  **cannot stand alone** under the 100-line floor; identity is the nearest concern by shape,\n  and the module already banners signing apart from the write path.\n- **`_lib_writes.py` keeps 1+3** — genesis and the status state machine.\n\nThe plan of record extracted only 4+5+6 and left `_lib_writes` at ~544 — sound at 778, but at\n800 that lands **above** the 200-500 target band on a file that grew 22 lines in weeks. Hence\ntwo cuts.\n\nMoved names are **re-exported** from `_lib_writes` with `# noqa: F401`, exactly as `fsck.py`\nre-exports from `fsck_scan`/`fsck_tracker_health`. That leaves `__init__.py` and `_lib_gates.py`\n**untouched**, so every `rebar.<name>` and `rebar._lib_writes.<name>` path survives — a smaller\ndiff than re-pointing consumers.\n\n**The pre-move surface, reconciled.** `_lib_writes` has 29 `def` statements = **27 distinct\nnames** plus the two extra `@overload` stubs of `create_ticket`. `__init__.py` re-exports\n**all 27**, so the facade surface and the definition set coincide — no name defined here is\nomitted from the facade. `_python_leaf` is one of the 27: it resolves as **`rebar._python_leaf`**\n(its own `_python_leaf as _python_leaf` alias in `__init__.py`) *and* as\n`rebar._lib_writes._python_leaf`, the form `_lib_gates.py` imports. The 27 partition across the\nconcerns above as 3 + 7 + 3 + 8 (leaf mutations, counting `_python_leaf`) + 2 + 2 + 2. Dependency direction is one-way — `_lib_writes` imports both new\nmodules, neither imports back — so there is no cycle.\n\nThis is **behaviour-preserving**: bodies relocate byte-identically; no logic is rewritten.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/_lib_mutations.py` (new) — concerns 4+5+6\n- `src/rebar/_lib_identity.py` (new) — concerns 2+7\n- `src/rebar/_lib_writes.py` — keeps 1+3, gains the two re-export blocks\n\n`__init__.py`, `_lib_gates.py`, and everything under `tests/` are deliberately **not** touched.\nThe reference audit supports that: the only real-code importers of `_lib_writes` are\n`_lib_gates.py` (`_python_leaf`) and `__init__.py` (the 27-name re-export), and the string pass\n(`monkeypatch.setattr` / `getattr` / `importlib`) finds **zero** `_lib_writes` attribute\nreferences — every test patch targets the `rebar` facade or `rebar.signing`, both preserved.\n\n`.github/complexity-baseline.json` holds **zero** entries for `_lib_writes.py`, so no moved\nsymbol carries accepted debt and the `--lock` re-key hazard that cast `Verified -1` on the\n`fsck` change cannot arise. The baseline is therefore not in scope.\n\n## Testing\n\nNo new behaviour, so the oracle is the existing suite passing with **no test file edited**. The\nspecific risk is the **public API surface**, since all 27 names are re-exported as\n`rebar.<name>` and `_lib_gates` depends on `_python_leaf` at three call sites — a silently dropped re-export\nwould still leave the suite green wherever the facade is imported lazily. Checked by name:\n\n- every name previously importable as `rebar.<name>` still resolves after the move, asserted\n  name by name against the pre-move list;\n- `rebar._lib_writes.<name>` still resolves for all moved names, which is what makes\n  `_lib_gates` and any `monkeypatch` target survive;\n- the three modules import cleanly in **either** order, catching a cycle introduced by the\n  re-export direction.\n\n`tests/unit/test_module_size_contract.py` is the size oracle and needs no edit.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] `_lib_writes.py` is at or below 450 lines; checked by\n      `[ \"$(wc -l < src/rebar/_lib_writes.py)\" -le 450 ]` exiting 0.\n- [x] `_lib_mutations.py` is between 100 and 500 lines inclusive; checked by an exit-code\n      comparison on `wc -l < src/rebar/_lib_mutations.py`.\n- [x] `_lib_identity.py` is between 100 and 500 lines inclusive; checked by an exit-code\n      comparison on `wc -l < src/rebar/_lib_identity.py`.\n- [x] The repo's size oracle still passes; checked by\n      `pytest tests/unit/test_module_size_contract.py` exiting 0.\n- [x] All 27 names still resolve on the facade as `rebar.<name>` — 26 public wrappers plus\n      `rebar._python_leaf`; checked by a script asserting `hasattr(rebar, n)` for every name in\n      the pre-move list, exiting non-zero on the first miss.\n- [x] All 27 names still resolve as `rebar._lib_writes.<name>`, which is the form\n      `_lib_gates.py` imports; checked by the same assert-and-exit script against\n      `rebar._lib_writes`.\n- [x] `src/rebar/__init__.py` and `src/rebar/_lib_gates.py` are unchanged; checked by\n      `git diff --exit-code HEAD~1 -- src/rebar/__init__.py src/rebar/_lib_gates.py` exiting 0.\n- [x] No file under `tests/` is changed; checked by `git diff --name-only HEAD~1 -- tests/`\n      producing empty output.\n- [x] The three modules import cleanly in any order; checked by two fresh interpreters, one\n      importing `_lib_identity`, `_lib_mutations`, `_lib_writes` in that order and one in\n      reverse, both exiting 0.\n- [x] `make lint` is green; checked by it exiting 0.\n- [x] `make typecheck` is green; checked by it exiting 0.\n- [x] The CI test selection passes; checked by\n      `pytest -m \"not integration and not external\"` exiting 0.\n- [x] `scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --lock` reports no new entries; checked by running\n      it with `GITHUB_REPOSITORY=navapbc/rebar` and confirming exit 0."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786656747204622001,"uuid":"87d67ce8-be5d-430d-a6e3-1f1312672bc7"}